# the vase clocks' occluder records marked off (SPEC.md 130.53): every record a vase cuts hides a ball only in the
# VOID cells behind it - a ball there is falling off an edge, never behind a clock in play - so those cells cut
# none (the start's clock at (7, 13) cuts none already: the noocclude round A, below)
noocclude rect 23 43 24 47   # behind the finish's (24, 46): the void between V's ramp and the windmill floor
noocclude rect 24 44 25 46
noocclude rect 19 23 21 26   # behind (21, 25): the void west of the ramp below the see-saw
noocclude rect 21 23 22 25
noocclude rect 32 33 34 36   # behind (34, 35): the void west and north of its pillar
noocclude rect 34 33 35 35

